<title>JAPAN: NTT to cut workforce to 150,000 by 2001.</title>
<headline>NTT to cut workforce to 150,000 by 2001.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) said on Wednesday that it would cut its workforce to 150,000 by the end of the year to March 31, 2001 from 185,000 at the end of March 1996.  </p>
<p>The planned cut in NTT's workforce is part of the company's overall review of its operations, NTT said in a statement.</p>
<p>NTT is reviewing its telephone directory enquiry service, sales and maintenance activities, and operations related to software development, it said without elaborating.</p>
</text>
